{"type":"message","id":"88cc1002","parentId":"fbeabfbd","timestamp":"2026-03-08T22:04:39.588Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Sun 2026-03-08 23:04 GMT+1] You are DeepSeek v3.2, an expert AI architect.\n\n**Context:** \n- OpenClaw has a Python neuro-memory-agent (8 brain mechanisms: Bayesian surprise, event segmentation, two-stage retrieval, consolidation, forgetting, interference resolution, online learning)\n- Currently NOT active - just sitting at /Users/tolga/Desktop/neuro-memory-agent\n- Evolution service exists but uses simple template-based proposals\n- User wants to wire neuro-memory to evolution for smarter proposals\n- **Problem:** Python IPC is slow. Can't compute Bayesian surprise on every event emit()\n\n**Question:** How should we integrate neuro-memory-agent into OpenClaw's evolution system?\n\nConstraints:\n1. Must not slow down hot path (event emit, tool execution)\n2. Should help evolution learn from past failures\n3. Can use batch queue (already implemented - 10 events / 2s flush)\n4. Only 1 evolution run per week typically\n\nGive me:\n- Architecture pattern (where to wire)\n- Performance strategy (async? batch? selective?)\n- Code sketch for integration\n- Trade-offs\n\nBe specific and opinionated."}],"timestamp":1773007479587}}
{"type":"message","id":"00693326","parentId":"88cc1002","timestamp":"2026-03-08T22:06:39.223Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me think through this systematically. The user wants to integrate a Python neuro-memory-agent into OpenClaw's evolution system without slowing down the hot path. Let me break down the constraints and requirements:\n\n1. **Hot path constraint**: Event emit() and tool execution must not be slowed down\n2. **Learning goal**: Help evolution learn from past failures\n3. **Batch queue available**: 10 events / 2s flush already exists\n4. **Low frequency**: Evolution runs ~1x per week\n\nFirst, let me understand the architecture:\n\n**Neuro-memory-agent** has 8 brain mechanisms:\n- Bayesian surprise (computationally expensive - probability distributions)\n- Event segmentation (detecting boundaries)\n- Two-stage retrieval (fast + slow retrieval)\n- Consolidation (converting short-term → long-term)\n- Forgetting (decay curves)\n- Interference resolution (handling conflicting memories)\n- Online learning (updating weights)\n\n**Evolution system** currently:\n- Simple template-based proposals\n- Runs infrequently (~1x per week)\n- Needs smarter proposals based on past failures\n\n**Key insight**: Evolution is NOT on the hot path. It runs asynchronously, infrequently. So the neuro-memory integration doesn't need to be synchronous with event emission.\n\n**Architecture pattern**:\n\nThe batch queue is already implemented and flushes every 2s or when 10 events accumulate. This is PERFECT for neuro-memory integration. Here's why:\n\n1. Events flow into batch queue (existing)\n2. Batch flush triggers neuro-memory processing (async, non-blocking)\n3. Neuro-memory updates its internal state (Bayesian surprise, consolidation, etc.)\n4. When evolution runs (1x per week), it queries neuro-memory for insights\n5. Neuro-memory provides learned patterns, failure modes, context for proposals\n\n**Performance strategy**:\n\n\nI'll focus on a non-blocking approach that maximizes system efficiency. By keeping event emit() lightweight and processing neuro-memory asynchronously, we maintain system responsiveness. The key is to leverage the existing batch queue, allowing neuro-memory to update in the background without impacting core system performance.\n\n**Code architecture** will involve creating a dedicated service that sits between the event queue and the neuro-memory system, ensuring smooth, decoupled integration. The service will handle batch processing, state updates, and provide an intelligent query interface for the evolution system.\n\n**Trade-offs** reveal a strategic compromise: accepting slight data staleness in exchange for improved system reliability and performance. The approach prioritizes background processing and intelligent data management over real-time, immediate updates.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"# Neuro-Memory + Evolution Integration Architecture\n\n## 🎯 Recommended Pattern: **Async Observer with Lazy Evaluation**\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                     HOT PATH (Fast)                         │\n│  Event → emit() → Batch Queue (10/2s) → Fire-and-forget    │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                            ↓\n                  ┌──────────────────────┐\n                  │  Async Batch Flush   │  (Every 2s, background)\n                  └──────────────────────┘\n                            ↓\n        ┌───────────────────────────────────────────┐\n        │     Neuro-Memory Service (Python)         │\n        │  • Receives event batches via IPC         │\n        │  • Computes Bayesian surprise (batched)   │\n        │  • Updates segment boundaries             │\n        │  • Consolidates to long-term memory       │\n        │  • Runs in background process             │\n        └───────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                            ↓\n                  ┌──────────────────────┐\n                  │  Memory State Store  │  (SQLite/DuckDB)\n                  └──────────────────────┘\n                            ↑\n        ┌───────────────────────────────────────────┐\n        │     Evolution Service (Weekly Run)        │\n        │  • Queries memory for patterns            │\n        │  • Gets failure clusters, surprise events │\n        │  • Generates smarter proposals            │\n        └───────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 📐 Architecture Decisions\n\n### 1. **Wire at Batch Flush, Not Event Emit**\n\n**Why:** \n- Batch flush is already async (every 2s or 10 events)\n- Batch processing amortizes IPC overhead across multiple events\n- Hot path just pushes to queue (microseconds)\n\n**Where to wire:**\n```typescript\n// In event-batch-queue.ts (existing)\nasync flushBatch() {\n  const batch = this.dequeueAll();\n  \n  // 1. Normal processing (existing)\n  await this.sendToHandlers(batch);\n  \n  // 2. Neuro-memory integration (NEW - fire-and-forget)\n  this.neuroMemoryQueue.push(batch).catch(err => {\n    logger.warn('Neuro-memory enqueue failed', { err });\n    // Don't fail the flush - neuro-memory is non-critical\n  });\n}\n```\n\n### 2. **Dedicated Python Process with Message Queue**\n\n**Pattern:** Producer-Consumer with **Redis Streams** or **Unix Socket + msgpack**\n\n```typescript\n// TypeScript side (producer)\nclass NeuroMemoryClient {\n  private queue: RedisClient; // Or Unix socket\n  \n  async push(batch: EventBatch): Promise<void> {\n    // Fire-and-forget with minimal serialization\n    const payload = msgpack.encode(batch);\n    await this.queue.xadd('neuro-memory-events', '*', { data: payload });\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```python\n# Python side (consumer) - neuro-memory-agent/\nimport asyncio\nfrom aioredis import Redis\n\nclass NeuroMemoryConsumer:\n    async def process_batches(self):\n        while True:\n            # Block until batch available\n            batches = await self.redis.xread(\n                {'neuro-memory-events': '$'}, \n                block=5000,  # 5s timeout\n                count=10      # Process up to 10 at once\n            )\n            \n            for batch in batches:\n                # Compute Bayesian surprise (batch = amortized cost)\n                surprise = self.agent.compute_surprise(batch)\n                \n                # Update memory\n                self.agent.update_beliefs(batch, surprise)\n                self.agent.consolidate()\n```\n\n### 3. **Memory State Store: SQLite/DuckDB**\n\n**Why not in-memory?**\n- Evolution runs weekly → Python process might restart\n- Need persistence for long-term learning\n- Query support for evolution insights\n\n**Schema:**\n```sql\n-- Memory state (updated continuously)\nCREATE TABLE memory_events (\n    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n    timestamp REAL,\n    event_type TEXT,\n    surprise_score REAL,  -- Bayesian surprise\n    segment_id INTEGER,   -- Event segmentation\n    embedding BLOB,       -- For retrieval\n    metadata JSON\n);\n\n-- Failure patterns (extracted periodically)\nCREATE TABLE failure_patterns (\n    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n    pattern_type TEXT,    -- \"tool_failure\", \"timeout\", etc.\n    context JSON,         -- Leading up to failure\n    frequency INTEGER,\n    last_seen REAL\n);\n\n-- Consolidated insights (for evolution)\nCREATE TABLE evolution_insights (\n    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n    insight_type TEXT,    -- \"avoid\", \"prefer\", \"constraint\"\n    description TEXT,\n    confidence REAL,\n    evidence_count INTEGER\n);\n```\n\n---\n\n## ⚡ Performance Strategy\n\n### **Three-Tier Computation Strategy**\n\n| Computation | When | Where | Cost |\n|-------------|------|-------|------|\n| **Batch update** (incremental belief update) | Every 2s | Python process | ~10-50ms |\n| **Consolidation** (short→long term) | Every 6 hours | Background task | ~1-5s |\n| **Deep analysis** (pattern extraction) | Before evolution run | On-demand | ~10-30s |\n\n### **Critical: Only Compute Bayesian Surprise on Batches**\n\n```python\n# BAD - compute on every event (too slow)\ndef on_event(event):\n    surprise = compute_bayesian_surprise(event)  # 50-100ms\n    update(event, surprise)\n\n# GOOD - batch computation\ndef on_batch(events):\n    # Amortized across batch: 50ms / 10 events = 5ms/event\n    surprise_scores = compute_bayesian_surprise_batch(events)\n    for event, surprise in zip(events, surprise_scores):\n        update(event, surprise)\n```\n\n### **Selective Processing (Filter Trivial Events)**\n\n```typescript\n// TypeScript side - filter before sending to Python\nconst NEURO_MEMORY_EVENT_TYPES = new Set([\n  'tool_execution',\n  'error',\n  'evolution_proposal',\n  'user_feedback',\n  'session_start',\n  'session_end'\n  // Skip: heartbeat, ping, metrics, etc.\n]);\n\nasync flushBatch() {\n  const batch = this.dequeueAll();\n  \n  // Filter to relevant events only\n  const neuroRelevant = batch.filter(e => \n    NEURO_MEMORY_EVENT_TYPES.has(e.type)\n  );\n  \n  if (neuroRelevant.length > 0) {\n    await this.neuroMemoryClient.push(neuroRelevant);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 💻 Code Sketch\n\n### **File: `src/neuro-memory/client.ts`**\n\n```typescript\nimport { EventEmitter } from 'events';\nimport { spawn, ChildProcess } from 'child_process';\nimport Msgpack from 'msgpack-lite';\nimport { createConnection, Socket } from 'net';\n\nexport class NeuroMemoryClient extends EventEmitter {\n  private socket: Socket | null = null;\n  private pythonProcess: ChildProcess | null = null;\n  private isConnected = false;\n  private reconnectAttempts = 0;\n  \n  constructor(\n    private config: {\n      pythonScriptPath: string;\n      socketPath: string;\n      autoStart: boolean;\n    }\n  ) {\n    super();\n    if (config.autoStart) {\n      this.start();\n    }\n  }\n  \n  async start(): Promise<void> {\n    // Start Python process\n    this.pythonProcess = spawn('python', [\n      `${this.config.pythonScriptPath}/main.py`,\n      '--socket', this.config.socketPath\n    ], {\n      stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe']\n    });\n    \n    this.pythonProcess.stderr?.on('data', (data) => {\n      console.error('[NeuroMemory]', data.toString());\n    });\n    \n    // Wait for socket to be ready\n    await this.waitForSocket();\n  }\n  \n  private waitForSocket(): Promise<void> {\n    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n      const maxAttempts = 50;\n      const interval = setInterval(() => {\n        this.socket = createConnection(this.config.socketPath);\n        \n        this.socket.once('connect', () => {\n          clearInterval(interval);\n          this.isConnected = true;\n          this.reconnectAttempts = 0;\n          resolve();\n        });\n        \n        this.socket.once('error', () => {\n          this.reconnectAttempts++;\n          if (this.reconnectAttempts >= maxAttempts) {\n            clearInterval(interval);\n            reject(new Error('NeuroMemory failed to start'));\n          }\n        });\n      }, 200);\n    });\n  }\n  \n  /**\n   * Push event batch to neuro-memory (fire-and-forget)\n   * Non-blocking - returns immediately\n   */\n  async pushBatch(events: any[]): Promise<void> {\n    if (!this.isConnected || !this.socket) {\n      // Silently drop if not connected (graceful degradation)\n      return;\n    }\n    \n    try {\n      const payload = Msgpack.encode({\n        type: 'batch',\n        timestamp: Date.now(),\n        events: events.map(e => ({\n          type: e.type,\n          timestamp: e.timestamp,\n          data: e.data\n        }))\n      });\n      \n      // Write length prefix + payload (simple framing)\n      const length = Buffer.alloc(4);\n      length.writeUInt32BE(payload.length, 0);\n      \n      this.socket.write(Buffer.concat([length, payload]));\n    } catch (err) {\n      // Log but don't throw - neuro-memory is non-critical\n      console.warn('[NeuroMemory] Push failed:', err);\n    }\n  }\n  \n  /**\n   * Query neuro-memory for evolution insights\n   * This is called during evolution runs (weekly, async)\n   */\n  async queryInsights(query: {\n    type: 'failure_patterns' | 'surprise_events' | 'recommendations';\n    timeRange?: { start: number; end: number };\n    limit?: number;\n  }): Promise<any[]> {\n    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n      if (!this.isConnected || !this.socket) {\n        resolve([]); // Graceful degradation\n        return;\n      }\n      \n      const requestPayload = Msgpack.encode({\n        type: 'query',\n        query: query\n      });\n      \n      const length = Buffer.alloc(4);\n      length.writeUInt32BE(requestPayload.length, 0);\n      \n      // Create one-time response handler\n      const handler = (data: Buffer) => {\n        try {\n          const response = Msgpack.decode(data);\n          this.socket?.off('data', handler);\n          resolve(response.insights || []);\n        } catch (err) {\n          reject(err);\n        }\n      };\n      \n      this.socket.on('data', handler);\n      this.socket.write(Buffer.concat([length, requestPayload]));\n      \n      // Timeout after 5s\n      setTimeout(() => {\n        this.socket?.off('data', handler);\n        resolve([]);\n      }, 5000);\n    });\n  }\n  \n  async stop(): Promise<void> {\n    this.socket?.destroy();\n    this.pythonProcess?.kill();\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### **File: `src/neuro-memory/index.ts` (Integration)**\n\n```typescript\nimport { NeuroMemoryClient } from './client';\n\nlet neuroMemoryClient: NeuroMemoryClient | null = null;\n\nexport function initNeuroMemory(config: {\n  pythonScriptPath: string;\n  enabled: boolean;\n}): NeuroMemoryClient | null {\n  if (!config.enabled) {\n    return null;\n  }\n  \n  neuroMemoryClient = new NeuroMemoryClient({\n    pythonScriptPath: config.pythonScriptPath,\n    socketPath: '/tmp/neuro-memory.sock',\n    autoStart: true\n  });\n  \n  return neuroMemoryClient;\n}\n\nexport function getNeuroMemory(): NeuroMemoryClient | null {\n  return neuroMemoryClient;\n}\n```\n\n### **Wire into Event Batch Queue**\n\n```typescript\n// In event-batch-queue.ts\nimport { getNeuroMemory } from '../neuro-memory';\n\nconst NEURO_MEMORY_WHITELIST = new Set([\n  'tool_execution',\n  'tool_error',\n  'evolution_proposal',\n  'evolution_result',\n  'user_feedback'\n]);\n\nexport class EventBatchQueue {\n  async flushBatch(): Promise<void> {\n    const batch = this.dequeueAll();\n    \n    if (batch.length === 0) return;\n    \n    // 1. Normal handlers\n    await this.sendToHandlers(batch);\n    \n    // 2. Neuro-memory (async, non-blocking)\n    const neuroMemory = getNeuroMemory();\n    if (neuroMemory) {\n      const relevant = batch.filter(e => NEURO_MEMORY_WHITELIST.has(e.type));\n      if (relevant.length > 0) {\n        // Fire-and-forget - don't await\n        neuroMemory.pushBatch(relevant).catch(err => {\n          logger.warn('Neuro-memory push failed', { err: err.message });\n        });\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### **File: Python Side (`/Users/tolga/Desktop/neuro-memory-agent/main.py`)**\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport asyncio\nimport argparse\nimport struct\nimport msgpack\nimport os\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any\nimport sys\n\n# Add neuro-memory-agent to path\nsys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))\n\nfrom neuro_memory import NeuroMemoryAgent, Event, EventType\nfrom storage import SQLiteStorage\n\nclass NeuroMemoryServer:\n    def __init__(self, socket_path: str):\n        self.socket_path = socket_path\n        self.agent = NeuroMemoryAgent()\n        self.storage = SQLiteStorage('neuro_memory.db')\n        self.running = False\n        \n    async def handle_client(self, reader: asyncio.StreamReader, writer: asyncio.StreamWriter):\n        \"\"\"Handle incoming connection\"\"\"\n        try:\n            while self.running:\n                # Read length prefix (4 bytes)\n                length_data = await reader.readexactly(4)\n                length = struct.unpack('>I', length_data)[0]\n                \n                # Read payload\n                payload_data = await reader.readexactly(length)\n                message = msgpack.unpackb(payload_data, raw=False)\n                \n                if message['type'] == 'batch':\n                    await self.handle_batch(message['events'])\n                elif message['type'] == 'query':\n                    response = await self.handle_query(message['query'])\n                    writer.write(msgpack.packb(response))\n                    await writer.drain()\n                    \n        except asyncio.IncompleteReadError:\n            # Client disconnected\n            pass\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"Error handling client: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        finally:\n            writer.close()\n    \n    async def handle_batch(self, events: List[Dict[str, Any]]):\n        \"\"\"Process batch of events through neuro-memory\"\"\"\n        # Convert to neuro-memory Event objects\n        neuro_events = []\n        for e in events:\n            event = Event(\n                event_type=EventType(e['type']),\n                timestamp=e['timestamp'],\n                data=e['data']\n            )\n            neuro_events.append(event)\n        \n        # Process through neuro-memory agent\n        # This computes Bayesian surprise, segmentation, etc.\n        results = self.agent.process_batch(neuro_events)\n        \n        # Store results\n        for event, result in zip(neuro_events, results):\n            self.storage.store_event(\n                event=event,\n                surprise_score=result.surprise_score,\n                segment_id=result.segment_id,\n                embedding=result.embedding\n            )\n        \n        # Periodic consolidation (every 1000 events or 6 hours)\n        if self.storage.event_count() % 1000 == 0:\n            await self.consolidate()\n    \n    async def consolidate(self):\n        \"\"\"Run consolidation (short-term → long-term)\"\"\"\n        print(\"[NeuroMemory] Running consolidation...\")\n        self.agent.consolidate()\n        self.storage.prune_old_memories(max_age_days=30)\n    \n    async def handle_query(self, query: Dict[str, Any]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"Query neuro-memory for insights\"\"\"\n        query_type = query['type']\n        \n        if query_type == 'failure_patterns':\n            patterns = self.storage.get_failure_patterns(\n                time_range=query.get('timeRange'),\n                limit=query.get('limit', 10)\n            )\n            return {'insights': patterns}\n        \n        elif query_type == 'surprise_events':\n            events = self.storage.get_high_surprise_events(\n                threshold=0.8,\n                limit=query.get('limit', 20)\n            )\n            return {'insights': events}\n        \n        elif query_type == 'recommendations':\n            # Use neuro-memory's learned patterns to generate recommendations\n            recommendations = self.agent.generate_recommendations()\n            return {'insights': recommendations}\n        \n        return {'insights': []}\n    \n    async def run(self):\n        \"\"\"Start the server\"\"\"\n        # Remove old socket if exists\n        if os.path.exists(self.socket_path):\n            os.unlink(self.socket_path)\n        \n        self.running = True\n        server = await asyncio.start_unix_server(\n            self.handle_client,\n            path=self.socket_path\n        )\n        \n        # Make socket accessible\n        os.chmod(self.socket_path, 0o666)\n        \n        print(f\"[NeuroMemory] Listening on {self.socket_path}\")\n        \n        async with server:\n            await server.serve_forever()\n    \n    def stop(self):\n        self.running = False\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    parser.add_argument('--socket', default='/tmp/neuro-memory.sock')\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    \n    server = NeuroMemoryServer(args.socket)\n    \n    try:\n        asyncio.run(server.run())\n    except KeyboardInterrupt:\n        server.stop()\n```\n\n### **Wire into Evolution Service**\n\n```typescript\n// In evolution-service.ts\nimport { getNeuroMemory } from '../neuro-memory';\n\nexport class EvolutionService {\n  async runEvolution(): Promise<EvolutionResult> {\n    // 1. Query neuro-memory for insights\n    const neuroMemory = getNeuroMemory();\n    let insights: any[] = [];\n    \n    if (neuroMemory) {\n      // Get failure patterns from last 7 days\n      const failures = await neuroMemory.queryInsights({\n        type: 'failure_patterns',\n        timeRange: {\n          start: Date.now() - 7 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000,\n          end: Date.now()\n        },\n        limit: 20\n      });\n      \n      // Get high-surprise events (might indicate edge cases)\n      const surprises = await neuroMemory.queryInsights({\n        type: 'surprise_events',\n        limit: 10\n      });\n      \n      insights = [...failures, ...surprises];\n    }\n    \n    // 2. Generate proposals with neuro-memory context\n    const proposals = await this.generateProposals(insights);\n    \n    // 3. Record evolution run as event (for future learning)\n    await this.eventEmitter.emit('evolution_run', {\n      proposalCount: proposals.length,\n      insights: insights.length,\n      timestamp: Date.now()\n    });\n    \n    return { proposals, insights };\n  }\n  \n  private async generateProposals(insights: any[]): Promise<Proposal[]> {\n    // Use insights to generate smarter proposals\n    // Example: \"Avoid retries when timeout < 5s (learned from 12 failures)\"\n    const proposals: Proposal[] = [];\n    \n    for (const insight of insights) {\n      if (insight.pattern_type === 'tool_failure') {\n        proposals.push({\n          type: 'constraint',\n          description: `Avoid ${insight.context.tool} when ${insight.context.condition}`,\n          confidence: insight.frequency / 100,\n          evidence: `Learned from ${insight.frequency} failures`\n        });\n      }\n    }\n    \n    // Also run traditional template-based proposals\n    const templateProposals = await this.runTemplates();\n    proposals.push(...templateProposals);\n    \n    return proposals;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## ⚖️ Trade-offs\n\n### **✅ Pros**\n\n1. **Zero hot-path impact**\n   - Event emit just pushes to queue (µs)\n   - Python process is completely async\n   - Graceful degradation if Python crashes\n\n2. **Learns continuously**\n   - Every batch updates beliefs\n   - Consolidation runs in background\n   - Knowledge accumulates over weeks\n\n3. **Evolution gets smarter**\n   - Proposals backed by real failure data\n   - Avoids repeated mistakes\n   - Identifies edge cases via surprise detection\n\n4. **Resource efficient**\n   - Batch processing amortizes IPC overhead\n   - Selective filtering reduces load 80%+\n   - SQLite is lightweight and queryable\n\n### **❌ Cons**\n\n1. **Complexity**\n   - New Python process to manage\n   - Socket communication debugging\n   - Two codebases to maintain\n\n2. **Latency in learning**\n   - Events take 2-5s to reach neuro-memory\n   - Patterns emerge over hours/days\n   - Not suitable for real-time adaptation\n\n3. **Persistence management**\n   - SQLite DB grows over time\n   - Need pruning strategy\n   - Migration if schema changes\n\n4. **Failure handling**\n   - Python process might crash\n   - Socket might get stale\n   - Need restart/recovery logic\n\n### **🤔 Mitigations**\n\n```typescript\n// Add health checks and auto-restart\nexport class NeuroMemoryClient {\n  private startHealthCheck() {\n    setInterval(async () => {\n      if (!this.isConnected) {\n        console.warn('[NeuroMemory] Disconnected, restarting...');\n        await this.restart();\n      }\n    }, 60000); // Check every minute\n  }\n  \n  private async restart(): Promise<void> {\n    await this.stop();\n    await this.start();\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 📊 Expected Performance\n\n| Metric | Target | Reasoning |\n|--------|--------|-----------|\n| **Event emit overhead** | <1µs | Just queue push |\n| **Batch flush overhead** | <5ms | Async fire-and-forget |\n| **Python batch processing** | <50ms | Amortized across 10 events |\n| **Evolution query time** | <500ms | Weekly run, can afford it |\n| **Memory DB size** | <100MB | 30 days of events |\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Recommendation: Start Simple\n\n**Phase 1: Basic Integration (Week 1)**\n- Wire into batch flush (fire-and-forget)\n- Python process with socket listener\n- SQLite storage\n- Just compute surprise scores\n\n**Phase 2: Query Interface (Week 2)**\n- Add query support\n- Wire into evolution service\n- Extract basic failure patterns\n\n**Phase 3: Full Learning (Month 1)**\n- Enable all 8 brain mechanisms\n- Consolidation schedule\n- Advanced pattern extraction\n\n**Phase 4: Optimization (Month 2)**\n- Profile and optimize hotspots\n- Tune batch sizes\n- Add richer queries\n\n---\n\n## 🔑 Key Insight\n\n**Don't overthink the integration.** The batch queue is already there. Just hook into it and send data to Python. Evolution runs weekly - it can afford to wait 500ms for insights. The Python process can crash and restart without affecting anything.\n\nThe magic is in the **continuous learning** - every failure, every surprise, every edge case gets absorbed and remembered. By the time evolution runs, neuro-memory has weeks of context to draw from.\n\n**Golden rule:** Hot path = queue push. Everything else = background async. Evolution = lazy query. Keep it simple."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zhipu","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":3051,"output":5451,"cacheRead":11200,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19702,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773007479588}}
